    "https://jobs.montana.edu/postings/52607": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Montana State University Employment Opportunities | Registered Dietitian Nutritionist Skip to Main Content Jobs at Montana State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About MSU About Bozeman Benefits Academics Registered Dietitian Nutritionist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is not eligible for new sponsorship Position Details Position Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 27052 For questions regarding this position, please contact: Jamie Rizzuto 406.994.6130 jrizzuto@msubobcats.com Classification Title Dietitian Working Title Registered Dietitian Nutritionist Brief Position Overview The Registered Dietitian Nutritionist ( RDN ) for Bobcat Athletics will assist 15 NCAA Division 1 sports programs and rodeo and spirit squad programs to provide nutrition counseling and medical nutrition therapy to individual student athletes, teams and coaches. This position reports directly to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Student Services. Position Number 4M0283 Department Athletics Division Athletics Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Exempt Union Affiliation FOCUS-MFPE FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Eligible Salary $28.417 per hour, commensurate with experience, education, and qualifications Contract Type Classified Salary If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Registered Dietitian Nutritionist ( RDN ) for Bobcat Athletics will provide nutrition counseling and nutrition therapy and education to individual student athletes, teams and coaches. The dietitian will have ownership of the Fieldhouse and BAC fueling stations, managing them in an organized and food safe manner. This includes maintenance, stocking and distribution of nutritional supplements to approximately 400 student-athletes. The dietitian will make informed decisions regarding athletes’ nutrition, hydration and sleep, both in and out of season. Duties and Responsibilities Lead and manage all aspects of the Athletics Sports Nutrition Program to support student-athlete health, wellness, recovery, and performance. Provide individualized nutrition assessment, counseling, and medical nutrition therapy for student-athletes, including performance nutrition, body composition goals, food allergies, and other nutrition-related health concerns. Develop and deliver sport-specific nutrition plans and education related to fueling, hydration, recovery, competition, travel, and supplementation. Collaborate with coaches, athletic trainers, team physicians, strength and conditioning staff, and other performance professionals on and off campus to provide integrated care and optimize student-athlete performance. Oversee fueling stations and nutrition operations, including budgeting, purchasing, vendor relations, inventory management, food safety, and service delivery. Coordinate nutrition support for practices, competitions, training camps, and team travel, including pre- and post-competition meal planning and recovery strategies. Educate student-athletes and staff on NCAA regulations regarding dietary supplements, banned substances, and safe supplement practices. Collect and evaluate nutrition-related data to assess outcomes and enhance program effectiveness. Supervise graduate assistants, interns, and student employees and support their professional development. Participate in departmental planning, budget development, and strategic initiatives. Maintain current RDN credentials, licensure, and professional competencies. Perform other duties as assigned by the Deputy AD for SA Wellness and/or Director of Athletics. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelors of Science degree in Nutrition or related field. Registered Dietitian credential through Commission on Dietetic Registration. Experience working with sports teams developing and executing nutritional programs and providing education to coaches, staff and players/student-athletes. Experience communicating with numerous constituencies in a professional and effective manner. Experience managing staff Experience managing a nutrition and fueling station budget. Excellent written communication and customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Masters degree in Nutrition or related field. National Strength and Conditioning Certification ( CSCS or CSCCA ). Food service experience. Experience working in a NCAA Division 1 nutrition program. Understanding of NCAA and Big Sky Conference rules and regulations. The Successful Candidate Will This individual must possess high ethical standards, extreme attention to detail, integrity and a willingness to exhibit a strict adherence to NCAA , University and departmental rules and regulations. Must be willing to work as a team member with coaches, athletic staff, student-athletes and several institutional departments. Excellent budget management skills. Position Special Requirements/Additional Information This job description should not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities or requirements, but a general description of the job. Nothing contained herein restricts Montana State University’s rights to assign or reassign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time. Physical Demands To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily with or without reasonable accommodations. The requirements listed above are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. This position has supervisory duties? Yes Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Upon completion of a successful search. Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Applications will be: Screening of applications will begin on 8/17/2026 ; however, applications will continue to be accepted until an adequate applicant pool has been established. Special Instructions This position is not eligible for new sponsorship EEO Statement Montana State University is an equal opportunity employer. MSU does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSU provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University Human Resources 920 Technology BLVD, Suite A Bozeman, MT 59718 406-994-3651 humanresources@montana.edu Accessibility | Contact List | Directories | Jobs | Legal & Privacy Policy | Site Index Montana State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
